  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Proof', 'Prove that the square of any odd number is odd.', '(2n + 1)² = 4n² + 4n + 1 = 2(2n² + 2n) + 1, which is odd.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Proof', 'Prove that n³ − n is always divisible by 6.', 'n³ − n = (n − 1)n(n + 1), the product of three consecutive integers. One is a multiple of 3 and at least one is even, so the product is divisible by 6.', 7),
